From: pblsketch <239486537+pblsketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/30] fix(table): 첫 줄도 담지 못하는 저장 셀 높이는 첫 문단 위 여백을 품게 하고, 표 속성은 넘어온 테두리·배경만 바꾸며, 표만 든 쪽 첫 문단의 앞 간격은 쪽 원점이 아니고, 작게 적힌 표 뒤 흐름은 바깥 상자 끝에서 잇는다

Ported onto devel 7d06d5c70: four parts, three ported.
(1) Devel now measures a stored first paragraph with `cell_paragraph_spacing::paragraph_before().occupied_before()`, which already covers the stored vpos (the 700HU case). Only the remainder for cells whose declared height misses the first line is added: `cell_first_para_missing_lead` at the two measure_table_impl sites, and in table_layout.rs on content height, first-line start and `upper_clip_line_reservation`. Devel removed `hwpx_reset_first_lead`, so that guard is gone.
(2) Unchanged. Devel's #7608/#7661 still give one new BorderFill to every cell in setTableProperties. `create_border_fill_from_json` in devel already starts from `borderFillId`.
(3) Devel #8149 `stored_textless_float_box_origin` covers only a host whose sole control is the table, not a section-first paragraph that also carries SectionDef/ColumnDef. So the table-only branch moved into stored_page_origin.rs. It now only returns true when it matches and otherwise falls through to devel's checks (including `float_closes_next`). Both the paint Table arm and typeset's `seed_whole_table_column_origin` use it. The seed fn and `commit_deferred_table_anchor` gained a `styles` argument for that.
(4) Not ported. The outgrown-table flow end conflicts with devel's lane/exclusion push after empty paragraph floats: the following paragraph is pushed back to the outer box end, then its own space before is added. So the tool-written sample's next table stays 5.3px lower than Hancom; the Hancom-resaved sample matches.
